{"name":"Brushed Orange","hex":"#f8a060","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brushed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Roughened by rubbing with an abrasive brushes, especially as a finish.","Having been cleaned, tidied, or straightened with a brush."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of brush"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brushed"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orange (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is a Japanese science fiction manga written and illustrated by Ichigo Takano, aimed at both shōjo and seinen demographics. The series follows high schoolgirl Naho Takamiya, who receives a letter written by herself ten years in the future. She is tasked with keeping an eye on Kakeru Naruse, a transfer student whose mother committed suicide on his first day of school. It was first serialized in 2012 in Bessatsu Margaret manga magazine and later in Monthly Action."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cd/Orange_manga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(manga)","wikidata":"Q18788443"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour 